#
# Dependency overrides for uv pip compile.
# Use this to exclude transitive dependencies or force specific versions to
# resolve conflicts.
# Use impossible markers (sys_platform == 'never') to exclude packages entirely,
# in this case the wheels that depended on them will additionally need to be
# patched through MODULE.bazel to remove these dependencies.

# Exclude opencv-python-headless - conflicts with opencv-python which is
# required by many dependencies and of which it is a subset.
opencv-python-headless ; sys_platform == 'never'

# The custom Torch 2.7.0+cu128 wheel currently pulls in `nvidia-nccl-cu12==2.26.2`.
# On ComputeLab B200 systems, that NCCL version reproduces a long communicator
# initialization stall during the first multi-GPU collective, consistent with
# the behavior discussed in https://github.com/NVIDIA/nccl/issues/1646.
# Until the Torch build is refreshed with a validated NCCL dependency, force a
# known-good NCCL wheel.
nvidia-nccl-cu12==2.29.7
